msgctxt "#32300"
msgid "Build Manager saves the Kodi setup you like, and helps put it on your devices.\n\nWhat it does\n• Create Build saves your current setup\n• Install Build puts a saved build on a device\n• Update / Repair fixes what doesn't match\n• Build Status shows how things look\n\nGood to know\n• Your other add-ons are left alone\n• It is not a full backup of Kodi\n• Help explains each menu item"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32301"
msgid "• Everything eligible is included by default. Uncheck add-ons you do not want. Dependencies needed by kept add-ons are handled automatically.\n\n• The current skin is included unless you exclude it. Private settings are included by default and can be turned off. Private values are never shown; only supported configuration is captured.\n\n• Enter a build name, version and device label, then review and confirm Create Build. Your Kodi is not changed: Create only reads installed software and settings. Nothing is saved as a build unless capture succeeds."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32302"
msgid "Install Build applies a registered local build.\n\nWhat you will do\n• Choose a build and a declared device profile\n• See the changes before anything happens to Kodi\n• Choose only the offered missing-package options\n• Repository Current saves a package before review and shows its version\n• Skip leaves that add-on out, where allowed\n• Review and confirm Apply Build\n\nGood to know\n• Other add-ons are left alone\n• A changed plan needs your approval again\n• Kodi may need to be fully closed and reopened more than once\n• Restart required is not completion\n• Update / Repair remains unavailable"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32303"
msgid "Update / Repair fixes a device that no longer matches its build.\n\nWhat it does\n• Checks what is different\n• Fixes only the parts that need it\n• Does not reinstall everything\n\nWhat you'll do\n• Choose Review Changes\n• Look at the list\n• Apply the fixes you want\n\nGood to know\n• Your other add-ons are left alone\n• If nothing is different, nothing changes\n• Some settings may need a restart before they are finished"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32304"
msgid "Build Status tells you how your build is doing.\n\nWhat the labels mean\n• Healthy: everything matches\n• Changes Needed: some parts don't match\n• Restart Required: close and reopen Kodi to continue\n• Needs Attention: Build Manager needs your help\n• Not Fully Checked: some checks haven't run yet\n\nGood to know\n• An older result is not the same as a fresh check\n• Use Check Again to look again\n• Checking changes nothing"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32305"
msgid "A build is the setup you want. A device profile adjusts it for one device.\n\nWhat that means\n• One build can work on different devices\n• Each device can have its own settings\n• Build Manager shows the device before you apply anything\n\nGood to know\n• Saving a build again makes a new version\n• Older versions are kept\n• Shared copies leave out private settings\n• Build Manager keeps its builds in its own storage\n• The transfer folder is only for moving copies in or out"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32306"
msgid "Build Manager only changes what a build tells it to.\n\nIt does not\n• Uninstall your other add-ons\n• Change Kodi when you Create Build\n\nInstall and Repair can\n• Install add-ons that belong to the build\n• Turn those add-ons on or off\n• Change your skin\n• Restore supported settings\n\nGood to know\n• You see the changes before they happen\n• Some add-ons may stay off until their settings are restored and checked\n• Closing a window does not undo changes already made\n• If something is interrupted, Build Manager helps you finish safely"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32307"
msgid "Some changes only finish after Kodi starts again.\n\nWhat you'll do\n• Fully close Kodi\n• Open it again\n• Open Build Manager\n\nGood to know\n• Closing just the Build Manager window is not enough\n• Build Manager does not reopen Kodi for you\n• It remembers where it stopped and carries on\n• You may need to restart more than once\n• If it says Needs Attention, open the problem page instead of starting over"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32308"
msgid "If something goes wrong, start here.\n\nNeeds Attention\n• Open View Problem\n• Use the action it suggests\n• If there isn't one, close Build Manager and try again later\n\nCan't find an add-on\n• Add the saved version yourself, or check again\n• Only use another version if the build allows it\n\nSomething wasn't saved\n• See what is missing\n• Create a new version after you fix it\n\nCouldn't confirm the result\n• See what failed\n• Use Review Changes to try again\n\nRestart Required\n• Fully close Kodi and open it again\n\nGood to know\n• Don't delete saved progress\n• Don't turn add-ons on by hand to get past a problem\n• Private settings are never shown"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32309"
msgid "Build Manager 0.1.0\nFor Kodi, from eengert.\n\nGood to know\n• Kodi's System Information shows your Kodi version and device\n• Add-on ID: script.build.manager\n• Source: https://github.com/eengert/script.build.manager\n• Being listed for a device doesn't mean it has been tested\n• Private settings are never shown here"
msgstr ""

